 and built numerous brick buildings in Maryville including the Blount County Courthouse (which burned in 1906). The house is one of two best examples of Italianate architecture, along with the Peter Bartlett House, in Blount County. It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places (NRHP) in 1989. David Jones also built the county's only Second Empire style house on\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0182-c44c0fb9d4a8:d04\", \"text\": \"p. 1 . ^ The Cambrian V. 28 . Thomas J. Griffiths . 1908. p. 473 . ^ Wisconsin State Journal . David Atwood . July 22 , 1874 . ^ Madison City Directories . Brainerd . 1873 . ^ Madison City Directory . Pryor . 1875 . ^ Madison City Directory . Morrissey and Bunn . 1880 . ^ Madison City Directory . Donnellon and Kain . 1883 . ^ a b Cravens , Stanley H. ( 1983 ) . Capitals and Capitols in Early Wisconsin . Wisconsin Blue Book . { { cite book } } : CS1\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0182-c44c0fb9d4a8:d05\", \"text\": \"► October ( 27 ) ► September ( 25 ) ► August ( 27 ) ► July ( 26 ) ► June ( 26 ) ► May ( 27 ) ► April ( 25 ) ► March ( 27 ) ► February ( 24 ) ► January ( 27 ) ► 2017 ( 312 ) ► December ( 26 ) ► November ( 26 ) ► October ( 26 ) ► September ( 26 ) ► August ( 27 ) ► July ( 26 ) ► June ( 26 ) ► May ( 27 ) ► April ( 25 )\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"1832\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"The David Jones House, a historic home in Georgia, was built in 1832. It is known for its Greek Revival architecture.\"}"
